course: dictionary
lesson: 14205
title: Muddied: dirty and confusing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Sam muddied his knees when he slid into the goal.» Muddied means made dirty, or covered with mud. Muddy is the word, and muddied is its past tense. It can also be an adjective: «Her muddied trainers were by the door.»
explain: Muddy can also mean making something harder to understand. «The fake photo muddied the waters, and nobody knew what had really happened.» Here the waters are not wet, they are the facts, and muddied means made them confusing.
explain: To check the meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «Sam covered his knees with mud» still makes sense, you have the first meaning. If «The fake photo made the problem more confusing» fits, you have the second.
fact: Muddied means made dirty or covered with mud.
fact: Muddy is the verb; muddies, muddied and muddying are its other forms.
fact: «Muddied» can also be an adjective, as in «muddied boots».
fact: «Muddy the waters» means to make a situation more confusing, often on purpose.
fact: Context clues help: if the story is about mud on clothes, muddied means dirty; if it is about a problem or a story, it probably means confusing.
exercise: «The rain had muddied the path, so we walked slowly.» What does muddied mean here? | *Covered with mud | Made very cold | Washed clean and shiny | Painted bright red
exercise: Dad says, «Don't muddy the waters.» What does he mean? | Don't jump in the puddles | *Don't make the problem more confusing | Don't forget your coat | Don't speak so loudly
exercise: Find and copy the word that is a form of muddy in «Her muddied football kit went straight into the wash.» | wash | straight | football | *muddied
test: «The answer muddied the waters, and nobody knew the truth.» What does muddied the waters mean? | Made the water warm and clear | Dried out the ground | *Made the problem more confusing | Cleaned up the river
test: Which word is the past tense of muddy? | muddies | mudded | muddying | *muddied
exam: In which sentence does muddied describe a noun? | «They muddies the stream every week.» | *«Her muddied trainers were by the door.» | «Ravi is muddying the yard right now.» | «The dog muddied the carpet with its paws.»
